    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced, supporting a Hold stance. The long-term trend is intact (price 15.3% above a rising 200-day SMA at $159.35, properly aligned moving average stack) and the balance sheet is a fortress ($18.99B operating cash flow, $216.66B equity), favoring the bull. However, near-term technicals are weak \u2014 price sits below the 10-day EMA ($183.66 vs $184.07), the MACD histogram has halved in two days, relative volume is a tepid 0.75\u00d7, and the stock is flat over 20 days. Critically, the fundamental picture is incomplete (no revenue, EPS, margins, or AWS data) and sentiment/news/macro data is entirely unavailable, preventing either a confirmed BUY or SELL. The risk-reward is asymmetric to the downside near-term (+2.6% to resistance vs -4.0% to support), but selling a stock in a firmly established uptrend with a fortress balance sheet on short-term noise would be overreacting. I will maintain the position at a neutral weight and wait for a decisive trigger: a breakout above $188.5\u2013$189.5 on above-average volume (upgrade/add) or a breakdown below $176.4 on above-average volume (downgrade/trim).\n\n**Entry Price**: 183.66\n\n**Stop Loss**: 176.4\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral/benchmark weight; no leverage or concentrated sizing given unresolved technicals and incomplete fundamental data. Position sized to tolerate a move to the 200 SMA ($159.35, -13.3%) without a distressed exit.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
